      <div type="clause" n="13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 13</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-e"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.33"/><pb n="56" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon oðerne æt gemænan weorce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.34"/> óffelle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.35"/> ungewealdes, agife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.36"/> mon þa<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.37"/></hi> mægum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.38"/> þæt treow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.26"/>, ⁊ hi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.39"/> hit hæbben ær XXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.32"/> nihta of þa<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.37"/></hi> lande, oððe him fó se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.40"/> to se ðe ðone wudu age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="56" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.1"/> oþerne æt gemænan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.11"/> weorce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.2"/> offealle ungewealdes, agife mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.1"/> ðam magum ðæt triow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.12"/>, ⁊ hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.4"/> hit hæbben ær XXX nihta of ðæm<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.7"/> lande don, oþþe him fó to se þe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.2"/> þone wudu age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf man oðerne æt g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>mænan weorce offealle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.6"/> ungewealdes, agyfe man þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> magon þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> treow, ⁊ hí hit hæbben ær þrittig nihta of ðæm lande, oððe him fo to se ðe ðone wudu age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis alium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.30"/> in communi opere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.31"/> casu deiciat, reddatur lignum parentibus interfecti; et habeant hoc infra triginta dies<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.32-2"/> eductum de terra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.33-2"/> illa, uel habeat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.34-2"/> hoc cuius erit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Af_13.lnote.oe.27"/> nemus.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="70" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif mon oðerne æt gemænan weorce óffelle<ptr type="editorNote" n="21" target="#Af_13.attnote.fn.21"/> ungewealdes, agife mon þam mægum þæt treow, ⁊ hi hit hæbben ær XXX nihta of þam lande<ptr type="editorNote" n="22" target="#Af_13.attnote.fn.22"/>, oððe him fó se<ptr type="editorNote" n="23" target="#Af_13.attnote.fn.23"/> to se ðe ðone wudu age.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="15" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="308" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif mon oðerne æt gemænan weorce óffelle ungewealdes, agife mon þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mægum þæt treow, ⁊ hi hit hæbben ær XXX nihta of þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> lande, oððe him fó se to se ðe ðone wudu age.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn einer den andern unabsichtlich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_13.lnote.de.1"/> bei gemeinsamer Arbeit [des Holzschlags<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_13.lnote.de.2"/> durch den fallenden Baum] erschlägt, liefere man [der Eigenthümer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_13.lnote.de.3"/>] den Baum den Verwandten [des Verunglückten] aus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_13.lnote.de.4"/>; und sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_13.lnote.de.5"/> sollen ihn vor 30 Nächten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_13.lnote.de.6"/> vom Lande [fortgeschafft] haben, widrigenfalls jener, der das Gehölz besitzt, ihn nehmen darf.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone unintentionally kills another at shared work [of timber-felling, by the falling tree], let [the owner] hand over the tree to the kinsmen [of the victim]; and they are to have [removed] it from the land within 30 nights, otherwise the one who owns the woodland may take it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="71" ed="#attenborough"/>If one man kills another unintentionally, [by allowing a tree to fall on him] while they are engaged on a common task, the tree shall be given to the [dead man’s] kindred, and they shall remove it within 30 days from the locality. Otherwise, it shall be taken by him who owns the wood.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="412" ed="#whitelock"/>If at a common task a man unintentionally kills another [by letting a tree fall on him] the tree is to be given to the kinsmen, and they are to have it from that estate within 30 days, or else he who owns the wood is to have the right to it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="309" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone kills another accidentally [by felling a tree on him] while working together, let the tree be given to the kin [of the slain man], and they must take it from the land before 30 nights, or let the owner take it.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">neues Cap., überschrieben ähnlich der zweiten Hälfte der Rubrik B’s zu</hi> 12, <hi rend="italic">nur Ld; vielleicht also nur Lambarde’s und sicher nicht ursprüngliche Abtheilung</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">new cap., with a heading similar to the second half of B’s rubric to 12, only in Ld; thus perhaps a division made only by Lambarde, and certainly not original</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rc <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rc Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">offylleð <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">offylleð So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">agyfe <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">agyfe So Ld</seg></note>
