        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">fügt zu T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et added by T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> offælle.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to offælle.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zufall scheidet sich hier nicht von Fahrlässigkeit; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl; vgl.</hi> Frank <hi rend="italic">Casuelle Tötung</hi> 33. Der Getötete hat mitgefällt; wohl deshalb bleibt sowohl Straf- wie Wergeld fort; <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> dagegen <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Absicht 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Accident is not distinguished here from negligence; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi>; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Frank <hi rend="italic">Casuelle Tötung</hi> 33. The man killed had shared in the felling; probably for that reason both fine and wergild are omitted; <hi rend="italic">see</hi>, on the other hand, <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Absicht 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Baum 6. Unabsichtliche Tötung bei gemeinschaftlichem Holzfällen, aber durch abfliegende Axt, kennt Deuteron. 19. 5, welche Stelle Ælfred in Gregorii <hi rend="italic">Cura</hi> ed. Sweet 16 übersetzt hatte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Baum 6. Accidental killing during joint tree-felling, but by an axe flying off, is dealt with in Deuteron. 19. 5, a passage that Ælfred had translated in Gregorii <hi rend="italic">Cura</hi> ed. Sweet 16</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dass Eigentümer mit überlebendem Holzhauer identisch, hält Ernst Mayer (<hi rend="italic">Lex Ribuar.</hi> 123) für möglich. Dann hätte wohl Af zum Schlusse ‘er’ statt der 4 letzten Worte gesagt. Q versteht einen Dritten; ebenso Kemble <hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> I 26, Brunner <hi rend="italic">Absichtl. Missetat</hi> 27. Unter dem Grundeigentümer (Grossbesitzer) arbeiten Holzhauer für Lohn oder Hintersassen auf seinem Gute</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ernst Mayer (<hi rend="italic">Lex Ribuar.</hi> 123) considers it possible that the owner is identical with the surviving woodcutter. In that case Af would probably have said ‘he’ at the end instead of the last 4 words. Q understands a third party; so too Kemble <hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> I 26, Brunner <hi rend="italic">Absichtl. Missetat</hi> 27. Under the landowner (great landholder), woodcutters work for wages, or tenants on his estate</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Durch Auslieferung der unbelebten Todesursache (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi>) entgeht ihr Eigentümer der Haftung (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 4. 5), die er sonst trüge wie für verletzende Waffen oder Tiere, die ihm gehören. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Brunner II 557</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">By handing over the inanimate cause of death (see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi>), its owner escapes the liability (see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4. 5) that he would otherwise bear, as for wounding weapons or animals belonging to him. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Brunner II 557</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Frist will nicht, wie Mayer meint, den Eigentümer mit Wergeldpflicht bedrohen, falls er nicht den Baum freigebe; denn dieser galt ja unendlich weniger als das Wergeld. Sondern sie will das Holzholen aus fremdem Walde zeitlich beschränken. — H’s Lesart bedeutet: ‘faciant educere’; ähnlich Q</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The time limit is not intended, as Mayer thinks, to threaten the owner with liability for the wergild should he not release the tree; for the tree was of course worth infinitely less than the wergild. Rather, it is intended to limit in time the fetching of wood from another man’s forest. — H’s reading means ‘faciant educere’; similarly Q</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_13.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hn 90, 6 schreibt anfangs Q ab, verwirrt aber dann Af 13 mit Lex Ribuar. 70, 1; mit dem Q-Verfasser identisch, benutzt er laut <hi rend="italic">noctes</hi>⁸² dessen Agsächs. Vorlage</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hn 90, 6 at first copies Q, but then confuses Af 13 with Lex Ribuar. 70, 1; being identical with the author of Q, he uses, as <hi rend="italic">noctes</hi>⁸² shows, the latter’s Anglo-Saxon exemplar</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_13.attnote.fn.21" n="21" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>óffelle</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">offealle</hi>. B, H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_13.attnote.fn.22" n="22" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>lande</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">lande don</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_13.attnote.fn.23" n="23" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>se</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">om. H, B, Ld &amp; So.</seg></note>
